"Функции аккордов" = "Chord functions";
"Справка: функции аккордов" = "Tonic function creates stability, predominant function prepares motion, and dominant function tends toward the tonic. In major: I, iii, and vi are T; ii and IV are S; V and vii° are D.\n\nIn functional minor, V and vii° use the raised seventh degree. The v and bVII chords belong to natural minor and have a weaker or different dominant function.";
"Обозначения ступеней" = "Degree notation";
"Модальные обозначения" = "Modal notation";
"Справка: модальные обозначения" = "Roman numerals are written relative to the parallel major scale: b lowers a degree and # raises it. Uppercase means a major triad, lowercase a minor triad, and ° a diminished triad.\n\nColors help compare chord stability within a mode, but they are not universal functions across every musical style.";
"Гармонические прогрессии" = "Chord progressions";
"Заимствованные аккорды" = "Borrowed chords";
"Заимствование" = "Borrowed harmony";
"Справка: заимствованные аккорды" = "Some progressions intentionally use chords outside the selected mode through modal mixture, secondary dominants, or the raised seventh in minor. These are common ways to strengthen harmonic motion.\n\nRoman-numeral accidentals are measured against the parallel major scale. Ratings reflect practical popularity and can be changed by the user.";
"Надстройки аккорда" = "Chord extensions";
"Справка: надстройки аккорда" = "The 9th, 11th, and 13th are normally added to seventh chords and written in parentheses, as in C7(b9) or Cmaj7(#11). A slash indicates an alternate bass note: C/E.\n\nAdded-note triads use symbols such as Cadd9, Cadd11, and C6. The symbol C13 implies that a seventh is present.";
